      {
        "description": "This folder contains Excel (.csv) and R (.Rdata) files of the three endobenthos datasets (2017 campaign, 2019 campaign, MWTL survey). The content of the Excel and R files are completely equal. Each dataset contains the following information: a unique station-number (“Station”), the date the sample was collected (“Sampling_Date”), the location of each station (“Longitude” and “Latitude”, in ETRS89 UTM31-projection), the video-based assigned habitat type (“HabitatType”, see section 2.5.2.), the WORMS-validated scientific name of the species (“Species”) and the corresponding total number of observations and density (m-2) at that station (“NrObserved” and “Density” respectively). The sampled area per station is ±0.2121 m2 in 2017 and ±0.0707 m2 for the 2019 campaign and the MWTL survey. In addition, the 2019 dataset also includes the column “SurveyArea”, which gives a broad description of the sampling location with respect to the large-scale tidal ridge troughs (“West”, “East N”, or “East S”).",
        "label": "Endobenthos_Data.zip",
        "restricted": false,
        "version": 2,
        "datasetVersionId": 3321,
        "dataFile": {
          "id": 46866,
          "persistentId": "",
          "filename": "Endobenthos_Data.zip",
          "contentType": "application/zip",
          "friendlyType": "ZIP Archive",
          "filesize": 25129,
          "description": "This folder contains Excel (.csv) and R (.Rdata) files of the three endobenthos datasets (2017 campaign, 2019 campaign, MWTL survey). The content of the Excel and R files are completely equal. Each dataset contains the following information: a unique station-number (“Station”), the date the sample was collected (“Sampling_Date”), the location of each station (“Longitude” and “Latitude”, in ETRS89 UTM31-projection), the video-based assigned habitat type (“HabitatType”, see section 2.5.2.), the WORMS-validated scientific name of the species (“Species”) and the corresponding total number of observations and density (m-2) at that station (“NrObserved” and “Density” respectively). The sampled area per station is ±0.2121 m2 in 2017 and ±0.0707 m2 for the 2019 campaign and the MWTL survey. In addition, the 2019 dataset also includes the column “SurveyArea”, which gives a broad description of the sampling location with respect to the large-scale tidal ridge troughs (“West”, “East N”, or “East S”).",
          "storageIdentifier": "surf://store:17685578b9a-189ee325ffe8",
          "rootDataFileId": -1,
          "md5": "677ada5408e87e426f39a3bb40ff01cb",
          "checksum": {
            "type": "MD5",
            "value": "677ada5408e87e426f39a3bb40ff01cb"
          },
          "tabularData": false,
          "creationDate": "2020-12-21",
          "publicationDate": "2021-04-06",
          "fileAccessRequest": false
        }
      },
      {
        "description": "This folder contains the raw video footage of all video transects for both the 2017 and the 2019 campaign, together with the dataset used in analysis. This is a second-step reporting of all valid footage, registering both organism occurrence and defined habitat type. The datasets are presented in both Excel (.csv) and R (.Rdata) format, without having any difference between them. The datasets comprise information on the associated video-file (“FileName”), the date-time stamp of the video used to link to the GPS position of the vessel (“Timestamp”, see section 2.4.3. and “Longitude” and “Latitude”, in ETRS89 UTM31-projection). It also contains a column “GridID”, in which each filming location is matched to a defined grid for the determination of observed survey area (See section 2.4.3.). Based on the unique number of grid cells and their resolution, one can determine the total observed area. For each second of valid video footage, the assigned habitat type is reported (“Habitat”), while for every organism, the identification and total number is stated (“Species” and “NrObserved” respectively). For the 2019 dataset, a broad description of the sampling location is given with respect to the large-scale tidal ridge troughs (“West”, “East N”, or “East S”). NB: The associated video files are available separately due to file size.",
        "label": "Epifauna_Data.zip",
        "restricted": false,
        "version": 2,
        "datasetVersionId": 3321,
        "dataFile": {
          "id": 46880,
          "persistentId": "",
          "filename": "Epifauna_Data.zip",
          "contentType": "application/zip",
          "friendlyType": "ZIP Archive",
          "filesize": 677802,
          "description": "This folder contains the raw video footage of all video transects for both the 2017 and the 2019 campaign, together with the dataset used in analysis. This is a second-step reporting of all valid footage, registering both organism occurrence and defined habitat type. The datasets are presented in both Excel (.csv) and R (.Rdata) format, without having any difference between them. The datasets comprise information on the associated video-file (“FileName”), the date-time stamp of the video used to link to the GPS position of the vessel (“Timestamp”, see section 2.4.3. and “Longitude” and “Latitude”, in ETRS89 UTM31-projection). It also contains a column “GridID”, in which each filming location is matched to a defined grid for the determination of observed survey area (See section 2.4.3.). Based on the unique number of grid cells and their resolution, one can determine the total observed area. For each second of valid video footage, the assigned habitat type is reported (“Habitat”), while for every organism, the identification and total number is stated (“Species” and “NrObserved” respectively). For the 2019 dataset, a broad description of the sampling location is given with respect to the large-scale tidal ridge troughs (“West”, “East N”, or “East S”). NB: The associated video files are available separately due to file size.",
